"new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ISHIBASHI, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KUBO, HIROAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIZOBE, MASAKAZU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOSHINO, HIROYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A preparation which can release a drug not in the stomach but quickly at the target site in the intestine when it is emitted from the stomach and, after a certain period of time, reaches the desired position. This preparation consists of a drug-containing core and a coating film comprising a mixture of a hydrophobic organic compound with an enteric polymer. By using this preparation, a drug can be selectively delivered to a specific site in the intestine, which makes it efficacious in, for example, topical treatments for digestive inflammatory diseases such as ulcerative colitis and Crohn's disease, and oral administration of peptide drugs which are liable to be chemically or enzymatically digested except for a specific site in the intestine, etc. or drugs which are absorbed exclusively at a specific site in the intestine.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Préparation pouvant libérer un médicament non dans l'estomac mais rapidement au niveau d'un site ciblé dans l'intestin quand ce médicament sort de l'estomac et, après une certaine durée, atteint la position souhaitée. Cette préparation consiste en un noyau contenant un médicament et en un enrobage contenant un mélange d'un composé organique hydrophobe et d'un polymère entérique. Cette préparation permet d'administrer un médicament de façon sélective à un site spécifique de l'intestin, ce qui la rend efficace pour, par exemple, des traitements localisés de maladies inflammatoires digestives, telles que la recto-colite ulcéro-hémorragique et la maladie de Crohn, ainsi que pour l'administration orale de médicaments peptidiques censés être digérés de façon chimique ou enzymatique sauf en ce qui concerne un site spécifique de l'intestin ou de médicaments absorbés exclusivement au niveau d'un site spécifique de l'intestin.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>